<title>SPAIN: Spain's Telefonica offers early retirement.</title>
<headline>Spain's Telefonica offers early retirement.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-04-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Telefonica de Espana said on Wednesday it had offered trade unions a new package for early retirement, reducing the minimum age to 55 years from 57.</p>
<p>But the Spanish telecommunications firm said it was not considering any new any plan to reduce its workforce.</p>
<p>&quot;It's still valid our plan to reduce our staff by 11,000 workers by 2001,&quot; a Telefonica spokesman said, commenting on a report in newspaper El Pais that Telefonica was planning to cut its workforce by 20,000 before the year 2001.</p>
<p>Telefonica had already denied similar reports in February.</p>
<p>At the end of 1996, Telefonica had 67,000 employees.</p>
<p>-- Madrid Newsroom, + 341 585 8340</p>
